    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The implementation is complete and the full test suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 1 test class \u2014 the only one in the project \u2014 passing).\n\n## What I changed\n\nFollowing the existing `bulkSignupWarning` pattern, I added a `capacityWarning` flag that's set to `true` when the owner's city already holds 40\u201349 owners (approaching the hard cap of 50). The existing 409 rejection at 50 (`CheckCityCapacity`) is untouched.\n\n1. **New pipeline function** \u2014 `rest/function/owner/FlagCapacityWarning.java`: counts existing owners in the owner's city (case-insensitive, same bucket as `CheckCityCapacity`) and sets `capacityWarning = count >= 40 && count <= 49`. It runs after `BuildOwner` (so the city is on the built owner) and before `SaveOwner` (so the new owner isn't self-counted).\n\n2. **Pipeline wiring** \u2014 `officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml`: inserted a `capacityWarning` step between `bulkSignup` and `save`, under `govern: [ transaction ]`.\n\n3. **Model** \u2014 `model/Owner.java`: added the `capacityWarning` field (`@Column(name = \"capacity_warning\")`) plus getter/setter. MapStruct auto-maps it into the DTO by name, so no mapper change was needed.\n\n4. **OpenAPI spec** \u2014 `openapi.yml`: added the read-only `capacityWarning` boolean to the `Owner` schema, which regenerates the `OwnerDto` field.\n\n5. **DB schemas** \u2014 added `capacity_warning BOOLEAN DEFAULT FALSE` to all four `schema.sql` files (h2, hsqldb, mysql, postgres).\n\nThe acceptance test `coreWarnsWhenApproachingCapacity` (fills a city with 40 owners, creates the 41st, expects `$.capacityWarning == true`) now passes.",
